# CONTROL for selector-field.go. When `pkg.Name` really IS a qualified type,
# joints reads it as one.
#
#   var_spec [32, 46)
#     name: identifier      "x"
#     type: qualified_type [34, 46)
#       package: package_identifier  "fmt"
#       name: type_identifier        "Stringer"
#
# Both trees, identical. This matters because the guilty witness produces a
# `qualified_type` too, and a reader could conclude joints has some general
# problem with `.` after a package name. It does not: in type position, where
# the grammar admits nothing else, it is right.
#
# The defect needs BOTH readings live at once, which only happens where an
# expression and a type are both admissible - go's declared
# `['qualified_type', '_expression']` conflict, exactly.
roots 1
mends 0
holds qualified_type
lacks call_expression
lacks type_conversion_expression
spans qualified_type 34 46
